        "original_id": "acb9d8cd-6b63-5305-9a93-c11ec86418a7",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: University of Florida, University of Texas System\n- People: Steven J. Kachelmeier, Harry Huntt Ransom\n- Places: Gainesville, Florida, Austin, Texas\n- Roles: university president, chancellor, faculty member, administrator\n- Topics: higher education, university systems\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Huntt Ransom was born on November 22, 1908, and died on April 19, 1976.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom was a faculty member and administrator at the University of Texas.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom became president of the University of Texas in 1960.\n- Harry Huntt Ransom served as Chancellor of the University of Texas System from 1961 to 1971.\n- The University of Florida is an American public land-grant, sea-grant, and space-grant research university.\n- The University of Florida is located on a 2,000-acre campus in Gainesville, Florida.\n- Steven J. Kachelmeier received his B.B.A. from the University of New Mexico.\n- Steven J. Kachelmeier received his Ph.D. from the University of Florida.\n- The University of Texas System is headquartered in Austin, Texas.\n- The University of Texas System has total enrollment of more than 216,000 students, making it the largest university system in Texas.\n- The University of Texas System employs more than 87,000 faculty and staff.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "fd2628ce-2025-5ed2-af23-1447abbd89cf",
        "text": "Page: University of Florida. Sentence: The University of Florida (commonly referred to as Florida or UF) is an American public land-grant, sea-grant, and space-grant research university on a 2000 acre campus in Gainesville, Florida.\nPage: University of Texas System. Sentence: The UT System is headquartered in Austin, and has a total enrollment of over 216,000 students (largest university system in Texas) and employs more than 87,000 faculty and staff.\nPage: Steven J. Kachelmeier. Sentence: Dr. Kachelmeier received his B.B.A. from the University of New Mexico and his Ph.D. from the University of Florida.\nPage: Harry Ransom. Sentence: Harry Huntt Ransom (November 22, 1908 – April 19, 1976) was a faculty member and administrator at the University of Texas, becoming the university's president in 1960, and ultimately served as the Chancellor of the University of Texas System from 1961 to 1971.",
